/**
 * Metadata engine M1 / E2: Crewflow's 21 workspace tables as Twenty-style STANDARD objects, plus the four read-only core
 * reference objects their relations point at (OWNER-METADATA-ENGINE.md §0.3 and §1 E2; mapping, locks and surprises S1–S13 in
 * docs/plans/phase-x4/M0-STANDARD-OBJECTS.md; owner decisions D1–D6 approved as recommended on 2026-11-13).
 *
 * Twenty (twentyhq/twenty @ eedb0a73) declares its standard objects in code in
 * `packages/twenty-server/src/engine/workspace-manager/twenty-standard-application/utils/object-metadata/` and
 * `utils/field-metadata/` (e.g. `compute-attachment-standard-flat-field-metadata.util.ts:37-45`). Re-implemented, not copied.
 *
 * ONE ENTRY PER COLUMN. Every column of every workspace table (except the tenant columns `organisation_id` / `workspace_id`,
 * which are never fields) is listed with its exact `format_type` and nullability, read from a freshly provisioned workspace
 * (structure level 21). The sync re-checks this list against `pg_catalog` of the target workspace at every run and refuses on any
 * difference, and `standard-objects-catalog.integration.spec.ts` checks it on every CI database, so a workspace command that
 * adds a column without adding it here fails.
 *
 * Locks (applied by the sync, not chosen here): every built-in field `is_locked`; `kind: 'system'` (the seven §0.3 objects) and
 * `kind: 'junction'` (S1) are `isSystem`, allow no custom fields and are read-only in every field; status columns are
 * read-only (S13); money (bigint pence) is read-only and sensitive (payroll.view).
 * Custom fields (owner decisions D1–D4): allowed on staff_profile, venue, job_role, shift, job_offer, shift_staff_review; not
 * on shift_assignment / venue_role_rate (D1, pay-rate tables), the junction tables (D3), shift_report / replacement_request /
 * user_note (D4), nor on any system object (§0.3).
 *
 * Names and API names are immutable once released (OB-10): change a label freely, never a `name`, `column` or `table`.
 * A pure data module: no I/O (upgrade-commands source guard).
 */
import type { StandardObjectDefinition } from '../../../../engine/metadata/standard-objects/standard-object-definition';
import type { StandardObjectDefinitions } from '../../../../engine/metadata/standard-objects/standard-object-sync';
import { WORKSPACE_TABLES } from '../workspace-tables';

